  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 1215 PM MDT Wed Sep 30 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nZonal flow aloft will continue throughout today, before weak \nridging begins to build off to the west tomorrow. This will allow \ntemperatures to remain seasonable today and tomorrow, with highs \nin the mid 60s to low 70s across much of the CWA. Some areas north\nof the Hi-Line will see cooler highs in the mid 50s. Light rain \nshowers will continue across Central/North-Central MT through this\nafternoon, dissipating as the evening approaches. \n\nFriday presents a similar situation, with weak ridging aloft \nallowing temperatures to continue to warm to highs in the 70s. A \nweak shortwave will move through Saturday, causing a brief \ncooldown in temperatures, before stronger ridging aloft builds on \nSunday. The upper level high pressure on Sunday and Monday will \ncause temperatures to rise, before an upper level trough moves in \nlowering temperatures back down to seasonably normal by the middle\nof next week. \n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nThe weather will be generally mild throughout the forecast \nperiod. However, there is the potential for fire weather concerns \non Monday. High temperatures in the 70s to mid 80s, minimum RH \nvalues in the teens to mid 20s, and winds gusting 20-30 mph are \nexpected. While at the moment nothing appears critical, we will be\nkeeping an eye on how these conditions progress. -Dzomba",
